<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00176</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dfbe91a7-480b-452b-ae56-85c1c0d66eb0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para>For questions 1 – 3, choose an equivalent equation.</para>
  
        <exercise id="b52a52a3-95d8-4b74-8c07-2cb024e1c0f1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which equation is equivalent to \(3x + 6 = 4x + 7\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(7x=1\)</para>
            <para>\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(9x=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
            <para>\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(3x-1=4x\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3x-1=4x\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_942bfea6-ff71-4594-9ff9-fe0e6d190ec5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which equation is equivalent to \(3(x + 6) = 4x + 7\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(7x=1\)</para>
            <para>\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(9x=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
            <para>\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3x+18=4x+7\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="fd402ad6-ad05-4fe4-ac10-b4a4ad5a6585" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which equation is equivalent to \(4x + 3x = 7-6\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(7x=1\)</para>
            <para>\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(9x=4x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
            <para>\(3𝑥=4𝑥+7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(7x=1\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(7x=1\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_64df16ad-469d-4280-8bcc-52d29d144939" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Select three equations that have 0 as a solution.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(2x+10=4x+10\), \(4x=9x\), and \(2x-3+4x=4-7\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \(2x+10=4x+10\), \(4x=9x\), and \(2x-3+4x=4-7\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="a05374c2-76ac-4ff2-99f4-8ddb1069cabc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which equation is equivalent to \(6(x-3)=24\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(6x-3=24\)</para>
            <para>\(x-3=4\)</para>
            <para>\(6x=21\)</para>
            <para>\(6x=27\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x-3=4\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(x-3=4\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_5764b7ed-1940-478d-8431-e5ca9c6ba19a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following sets of equations are equivalent to each other?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\)</para>
            <para>\(7(x+2)=21\) and \(7x +2=21\)</para>
            <para>\(5x - 2 = 7x +4\) and \(12x -2 =4\)</para>
            <para>\(6x-4=11\) and \(6x =7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\). Each side of the equation was divided
              by 5. So the equations are equivalent.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\). Each side of the
              equation was divided by 5. So the equations are equivalent. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_2fdde9ea-4d45-43f3-9578-2d046e7b548d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Using the distributive property, choose which equation would be an equivalent
              equation to \(3(x-2) =7\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(3x-2=7\)</para>
            <para>\(3x-6=7\)</para>
            <para>\(x-2=4\)</para>
            <para>\(3x=9\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(3x - 6 =7\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.7.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3x - 6 =7\). It is one of the solutions that could be
              equivalent to \(3(x-2) =7\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
